import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# The structure sheaf of the diagonal: finiteness, flatness, and `Δ_* = RΔ_*`

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a separated morphism of schemes with diagonal
`Δ = Δ_{X/S} : X ⟶ X ×_S X`.  Then `Δ` is a closed immersion, and

`𝒪_Δ = Δ_*𝒪_X`

is a quasi-coherent `𝒪_{X ×_S X}`-module of finite type, flat over `X` under either
projection; moreover `Δ_*𝒪_X = RΔ_*𝒪_X`.  These are the assertions of Example
[Stacks, Tag 0FYV] that precede its conclusion `Φ_{𝒪_Δ} ≅ 𝟭`, which is
`AlgebraicGeometry.fourierMukaiDiagonalKernelIso` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/DerivedVarieties/FourierMukai/DiagonalKernelIdentity.lean`.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.diagonalModule` — the `𝒪_{X ×_S X}`-module `𝒪_Δ = Δ_{X/S,*}𝒪_X`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.IsSeparated.isClosedImmersion_diagonal`, Mathlib's instance, which receives
  the tag of [Stacks, Tag 0FYV] here by `add_to_stacks` — `Δ` is a closed immersion.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.diagonalModule_isQuasicoherent` — `𝒪_Δ` is quasi-coherent.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.diagonalModule_isFiniteType` — `𝒪_Δ` is of finite type.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.diagonalModule_isFlatOver_fst` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.diagonalModule_isFlatOver_snd` — `𝒪_Δ` is flat over `X` under either
  projection.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.diagonalKernelIsoDiagonalModule` — `RΔ_*𝒪_X ≅ (Δ_*𝒪_X)[0]`, the source's
  identification `𝒪_Δ = Δ_*𝒪_X = RΔ_*𝒪_X`.

## Implementation notes

*Finite type.*  A closed immersion has locally surjective comorphism of structure sheaves, so
the canonical map `𝒪_{X ×_S X} ⟶ Δ_*𝒪_X` of `𝒪_{X ×_S X}`-modules is an epimorphism
(`Stacks.ClosedImmersion.epi_unitToPushforwardObjUnit_structureSheafHom`);
the structure sheaf is of finite type, being generated by the section `1`, and finite type
passes to quotients.  Finite type is Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`, which is
[Stacks, Tag 01B4]: locally generated by finitely many sections.

*Flatness.*  Flatness of a module over the target of a morphism of ringed spaces is
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsFlatOver`, flatness of every stalk over the corresponding stalk of the
target.  Off the image of `Δ` the stalk of `Δ_*𝒪_X` vanishes ([Stacks, Tag 00AE]), and a
trivial module is flat.  Over `Δ(x)` the stalk of `Δ_*𝒪_X` is the local ring `𝒪_{X,x}`, with
the action of `𝒪_{X, p(Δ(x))}` through the stalk map of `Δ ≫ p` ([Stacks, Tag 05B8], in the
form `AlgebraicGeometry.isFlatOverAt_pushforward_finite_iff`, applicable because a closed
immersion is finite with singleton fibres); so the assertion is flatness of `Δ ≫ p` at `x`,
and `Δ ≫ p = 𝟙_X` because `pr_i ∘ Δ = id_X`.  Both projections are treated at once, through an
arbitrary retraction `p` of `Δ`, in
`AlgebraicGeometry.diagonalModule_isFlatOver_of_retraction`.

*`Δ_* = RΔ_*`.*  Pushforward along a closed immersion is exact ([Stacks, Tag 08KS]), so the
derived direct image is the functor that `Δ_*` induces on derived categories
(`Stacks.ClosedImmersion.derivedPushforwardIsoMapDerivedCategoryOfSchemes`), and an exact
functor commutes with placing a module in degree zero
(`CategoryTheory.Functor.mapDerivedCategorySingleFunctor`).

*The model of the derived categories.*  As in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/DerivedVarieties/FourierMukai/Basic.lean`, the derived
categories are read at `CategoryTheory.HasDerivedCategory.standard`, given a raised local
instance priority so that the locally small model arriving with the imports does not compete.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FYV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FYV)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 00AE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00AE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01B4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01B4)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08KS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08KS)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

-- The priority selects the standard model of the derived categories, the one the diagonal
-- kernel of [Stacks, Tag 0FYV] is read at, over the locally small model arriving with the
-- imports.
attribute [local instance 100000] HasDerivedCategory.standard

/-! ### The structure sheaf of the diagonal -/

variable {S X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S)

/-- **The structure sheaf of the diagonal, [Stacks, Tag 0FYV]**: the `𝒪_{X ×_S X}`-module

`𝒪_Δ = Δ_{X/S,*}𝒪_X`,

the ordinary direct image along the diagonal `Δ : X ⟶ X ×_S X` of the structure sheaf of `X`.

This is the module the source's Example 0FYV writes `Δ_*\mathcal{O}_X`; its identification with
the derived direct image `RΔ_*𝒪_X`, which is `AlgebraicGeometry.diagonalKernel`, is
`AlgebraicGeometry.diagonalKernelIsoDiagonalModule`. -/
@[stacks 0FYV "the `𝒪_{X ×_S X}`-module `𝒪_Δ = Δ_{X/S,*}𝒪_X`"]
def diagonalModule : (Limits.pullback f f).Modules :=
  (Scheme.Modules.pushforward (Limits.pullback.diagonal f)).obj
    (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)

/- The opening assertion of [Stacks, Tag 0FYV], that the diagonal of a separated morphism is a
closed immersion, is the field `isClosedImmersion_diagonal` of Mathlib's class
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsSeparated`, an instance. -/
add_to_stacks 0FYV "the diagonal `Δ : X ⟶ X ×_S X` of a separated morphism is a closed immersion"
  AlgebraicGeometry.IsSeparated.isClosedImmersion_diagonal

/-- **`𝒪_Δ` is a quasi-coherent `𝒪_{X ×_S X}`-module**, part of the assertion of
[Stacks, Tag 0FYV].  The diagonal of a separated morphism is a closed immersion, hence an
affine morphism, and the direct image of the structure sheaf along an affine morphism is
quasi-coherent. -/
@[stacks 0FYV "`𝒪_Δ = Δ_*𝒪_X` is a quasi-coherent `𝒪_{X ×_S X}`-module, for `f` separated"]
theorem diagonalModule_isQuasicoherent [IsSeparated f] :
    (diagonalModule f).IsQuasicoherent :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineQcohPushforward.isQuasicoherent_restrictScalars_pushforwardRing
    (Limits.pullback.diagonal f)

/-- **`𝒪_Δ` is of finite type**, part of the assertion of [Stacks, Tag 0FYV].  Finite type is
Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType`, [Stacks, Tag 01B4]: locally generated by finitely many
sections.

The canonical map `𝒪_{X ×_S X} ⟶ Δ_*𝒪_X` is an epimorphism of `𝒪_{X ×_S X}`-modules, because
the comorphism of structure sheaves of a closed immersion is locally surjective; the structure
sheaf is of finite type, being generated by the single section `1`; and finite type passes to
quotients. -/
@[stacks 0FYV "`𝒪_Δ = Δ_*𝒪_X` is of finite type, for `f` separated"]
theorem diagonalModule_isFiniteType [IsSeparated f] :
    (diagonalModule f).IsFiniteType :=
  -- The two hypotheses of `isFiniteType_of_epi'` are supplied explicitly: each is available
  -- only at one of the two interchangeable spellings of the structure sheaf of a scheme, and
  -- instance search does not cross between them.
  @Stacks.SheafOfModules.isFiniteType_of_epi'.{u} _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _
    (SheafOfModules.unitToPushforwardObjUnit (Limits.pullback.diagonal f).toRingCatSheafHom)
    (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherenceCriteria.isFiniteType_unit (Limits.pullback f f))
    (Stacks.ClosedImmersion.epi_unitToPushforwardObjUnit_structureSheafHom
      (Limits.pullback.diagonal f))

/-- **`𝒪_Δ` is flat over `X` under a projection**, for either projection: the general step.
`p` is a morphism `X ×_S X ⟶ X` with `Δ ≫ p = 𝟙_X`, which both projections are.

Off the image of `Δ` the stalk of `Δ_*𝒪_X` vanishes ([Stacks, Tag 00AE]) and a trivial module
is flat.  Over `Δ(x)` the stalk of `Δ_*𝒪_X` is the local ring `𝒪_{X,x}` ([Stacks, Tag 05B8], in
the form `AlgebraicGeometry.isFlatOverAt_pushforward_finite_iff`, applicable because a closed
immersion is finite with singleton fibres), so the assertion is flatness of `Δ ≫ p = 𝟙_X` at
`x`, and the identity is flat. -/
theorem diagonalModule_isFlatOver_of_retraction [IsSeparated f]
    (p : Limits.pullback f f ⟶ X) (hp : Limits.pullback.diagonal f ≫ p = 𝟙 X) :
    IsFlatOver p.toLRSHom.toShHom (diagonalModule f) := by
  have : (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf).IsQuasicoherent :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineQcohPushforward.isQuasicoherent_unit X
  have : Flat (Limits.pullback.diagonal f ≫ p) := by rw [hp]; infer_instance
  intro w
  by_cases hw : w ∈ Set.range (ConcreteCategory.hom (Limits.pullback.diagonal f).base)
  · obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hw
    refine hx ▸ (isFlatOverAt_pushforward_finite_iff (Limits.pullback.diagonal f) p
      (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) x
      (preimage_singleton_of_isClosedImmersion (Limits.pullback.diagonal f) x)).mp ?_
    exact (isFlatOverAt_unit_iff_isFlatAt (Limits.pullback.diagonal f ≫ p) x).mpr
      (Flat.stalkMap (Limits.pullback.diagonal f ≫ p) x)
  · exact isFlatOverAt_of_subsingleton_stalk p (diagonalModule f) w
      (subsingleton_stalk_pushforward_of_notMemRange' (Limits.pullback.diagonal f)
        (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf) w hw)

/-- **`𝒪_Δ` is flat over `X` under the first projection**, part of the assertion of
[Stacks, Tag 0FYV]. -/
@[stacks 0FYV "`𝒪_Δ = Δ_*𝒪_X` is flat over `X` under the first projection, for `f` separated"]
theorem diagonalModule_isFlatOver_fst [IsSeparated f] :
    IsFlatOver (Limits.pullback.fst f f).toLRSHom.toShHom (diagonalModule f) :=
  diagonalModule_isFlatOver_of_retraction f _ (Limits.pullback.diagonal_fst f)

/-- **`𝒪_Δ` is flat over `X` under the second projection**, part of the assertion of
[Stacks, Tag 0FYV]. -/
@[stacks 0FYV "`𝒪_Δ = Δ_*𝒪_X` is flat over `X` under the second projection, for `f` separated"]
theorem diagonalModule_isFlatOver_snd [IsSeparated f] :
    IsFlatOver (Limits.pullback.snd f f).toLRSHom.toShHom (diagonalModule f) :=
  diagonalModule_isFlatOver_of_retraction f _ (Limits.pullback.diagonal_snd f)

/-! ### The ordinary and the derived direct image agree -/

/-- **`Δ_*𝒪_X = RΔ_*𝒪_X`**, the source's identification in [Stacks, Tag 0FYV]: for `f`
separated the diagonal kernel `𝒪_Δ = RΔ_*𝒪_X` of `AlgebraicGeometry.diagonalKernel` is the
ordinary direct image `Δ_*𝒪_X` placed in degree zero.

The diagonal of a separated morphism is a closed immersion, along which pushforward of sheaves
of modules is exact ([Stacks, Tag 08KS]); so `RΔ_*` is the functor `Δ_*` induces on derived
categories, and an exact functor commutes with placing a module in degree zero. -/
@[stacks 0FYV "`𝒪_Δ = Δ_*𝒪_X = RΔ_*𝒪_X`: the ordinary and the derived direct image of `𝒪_X` \
along the diagonal agree, for `f` separated"]
def diagonalKernelIsoDiagonalModule [IsSeparated f] :
    diagonalKernel f ≅
      (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (Limits.pullback f f).Modules 0).obj (diagonalModule f) :=
  (Stacks.ClosedImmersion.derivedPushforwardIsoMapDerivedCategoryOfSchemes
      (Limits.pullback.diagonal f)).app _ ≪≫
    ((modulePushforward
      (Limits.pullback.diagonal f).toLRSHom.toShHom).mapDerivedCategorySingleFunctor 0).app
        (SheafOfModules.unit X.ringCatSheaf)

end AlgebraicGeometry

end
